    "intro_html":  "A tagine is a slow braise built on warm spice instead of heat, and this one leans on cumin, turmeric, paprika, and cinnamon with golden raisins for sweetness and a squeeze of lemon to cut it. The chickpeas are the budget trick. They stretch the beef, add their own protein, and soak up the sauce. Each bowl runs {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
